hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"16308","Abdullah narrated to us: Ibrahim ibn al-Hajjaj al-Naji narrated to me, he said: Abd al-Qahir ibn al-Sari narrated to us, he said: A son of Kinanah ibn 'Abbas ibn Mirdas narrated to me, from his father, that his father al-'Abbas ibn Mirdas narrated to him, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) supplicated on the evening of 'Arafah for his ummah for forgiveness and mercy, and he supplicated much, so Allah, Mighty and Majestic, answered him: I have done, and I have forgiven your ummah except one who wronged another among them. So he said: O Lord, indeed You are able to forgive the wrongdoer and reward the wronged better than his wrong. But there was in that evening only that. Then when it was the next day, he supplicated in the morning of Muzdalifah, and returned supplicating for his ummah, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not remain but he smiled. So some of his Companions said: O Messenger of Allah, may my father and mother be ransom for you, you laughed in an hour in which you did not used to laugh, so what made you laugh, may Allah make your teeth laugh? He said: I smiled at the enemy of Allah, Iblis, when he knew that Allah, Mighty and Majestic, had answered me concerning my ummah and forgiven the wrongdoer, he fell to calling for destruction and woe and throwing dust upon his head, so I smiled at what he does from his anguish."
